ze how pathogenic proteins move  that's important in developing new  medications  brock learned to appreciate the value of  linking different fields of research in  the u.s  i think americans are much more  adventurous and willing to take risks  in contrast  germans like it when things are  structured  where there are rules that determine  everything  and especially in research where you  really need to be able to act freely and  react quickly to ideas  the american environment is ideal  the thing is the thumb has to despite  that brock returned to germany  this year to be fixed electricity he now  wants to implement that freedom in  research and non-hierarchical  organization in germany  a funded alexander von humboldt  professorship has enabled him to do so  it doesn't need to go through  the environment i'm helping to create  with this funding and the support of the  technical university is certainly an  unusually good environment for research  berlin was the right decision for oliver  brock and he has no intention of leaving
 

